# .linespec/hash_manifest.json is one compact JSON object per record per
# line, sorted by record ID (see pkg/provenance/hasher.go). Concurrent seals
# on independent branches almost always insert at different lines and merge
# cleanly with git's default 3-way merge; when two branches' new records
# happen to sort into the very same gap, git has no way to know which line
# should come first and reports a conflict. `merge=union` (a built-in git
# merge driver, no extra setup required) resolves that residual case safely
# by keeping every added line from both sides — safe here specifically
# because each line is a fully self-contained JSON object with no shared
# punctuation (no trailing commas, no wrapping array/object), so a union
# merge can never produce invalid JSON. See provenance/prov-2026-3687be46.yml
# (issue #163) for the conflict this replaced.
# **/ so nested package manifests (a config resolved via -c
# <path>/.linespec.yml gets its own manifest under <path>/.linespec/) are
# covered too, not just a root-level one.
**/.linespec/hash_manifest.json merge=union
